    "sourceSha256": "9e6abfb17f0982d1eb3ad03690e8f1a2e07434bb2a381f9a9d0981a482005fd0",
    "sourceWikitext": "__NOTOC__{{recipesummary|category=Bread recipes|servings=8|time=Prep: 15 minutes<br>Baking: 50-70 minutes|difficulty=2\n}}{{recipe}}| [[Cookbook:Cuisine of Ireland|Irish cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Vegetarian cuisine|Vegetarian Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Bread|Bread]]\n\nConventional bread, containing live yeast, leavens (rises) as the micro-organisms make carbon dioxide gas as a by-product of their metabolism. Similarly, soda bread utilizes the reaction between baking soda and vinegar, or some other acid, to make the bread rise through the production of carbon dioxide. This recipe uses buttermilk, or optionally a combination of milk and vinegar, but other recipes use sour cream.\n\n==Ingredients==\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* ⅛ cup [[Cookbook:White sugar|white sugar]]\n* 1 teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]], lightly [[Cookbook:Beat|beaten]]\n* 2 cups [[Cookbook:Buttermilk|buttermilk]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Butter|butter]], melted\n\n==Procedure==\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|325°F]] (160°C).\n# Grease and flour a 9x5-[[Cookbook:Inch|inch]] [[Cookbook:Loaf Pan|loaf pan]].\n# Combine flour, baking powder, baking soda, sugar, and salt in a large mixing bowl.\n# Blend egg and buttermilk together, and add all at once to the flour mixture.\n# Mix until just moistened. Too much mixing will make it tough.\n# Stir in butter; pour into prepared pan.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] for 65–70 minutes, or until a [[Cookbook:Skewer|toothpick]] inserted in the bread comes out clean. The loaf should sound hollow if you tap the base.\n# Cool on a [[Cookbook:Cooling Rack|wire rack]].\n# Wrap in tea-towel or [[Cookbook:Aluminium Foil|foil]] several hours or overnight for best flavor.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n* May serve [[cookbook:toast|toast]]ed and buttered.\n* Soda bread rises as a result of acid being mixed with baking soda. The acid is commonly in the form of vinegar, lemon juice, or buttermilk. A tablespoon of [[Cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]] or [[Cookbook:Vinegar|vinegar]] in one cup of milk can be substituted for each cup of buttermilk.\n* For best results, bake it at 375°F (190°C), for about 50 minutes, on a preheated baking stone.\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Irish recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for bread]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using butter]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using buttermilk]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]",
